{
  "description": "wrapToolOutput(content, {toolName, nonce, detect}). `output` is the returned {text, tag, forgedDelimiters, findings} — findings carry {signal, index, excerpt}, with `index` a UTF-16 code-unit offset into the original content — or {error: {kind, message}} when the nonce is refused. The tool name has every run of characters outside [A-Za-z0-9_.:-] replaced by one `_`. Delimiters are matched case-insensitively as `<` + optional `/` + the tag, and escaped by inserting a backslash after `<`. The delimiter_forgery finding, when present, comes first; then at most one finding per detection pattern, in pattern order. `detect` defaults to true.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "plain content",
      "input": {
        "nonce": "a1b2c3d4e5f60718",
        "toolName": "read",
        "content": "hello"
      },
      "output": {
        "text": "<tool_output_a1b2c3d4e5f60718 name=\"read\">\nhello\n</tool_output_a1b2c3d4e5f60718>",
        "tag": "tool_output_a1b2c3d4e5f60718",
        "forgedDelimiters": 0,
        "findings": []
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a tool name that would break out of the attribute",
      "input": {
        "nonce": "a1b2c3d4e5f60718",
        "toolName": "mcp_evil\"><script>",
        "content": "x"
      },
      "output": {
        "text": "<tool_output_a1b2c3d4e5f60718 name=\"mcp_evil_script_\">\nx\n</tool_output_a1b2c3d4e5f60718>",
        "tag": "tool_output_a1b2c3d4e5f60718",
        "forgedDelimiters": 0,
        "findings": []
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a tool name with every character the attribute keeps",
      "input": {
        "nonce": "a1b2c3d4e5f60718",
        "toolName": "mcp.github:issues-list_v2",
        "content": "x"
      },
      "output": {
        "text": "<tool_output_a1b2c3d4e5f60718 name=\"mcp.github:issues-list_v2\">\nx\n</tool_output_a1b2c3d4e5f60718>",
        "tag": "tool_output_a1b2c3d4e5f60718",
        "forgedDelimiters": 0,
        "findings": []
      }
    },
    {
